@flexiarg baldwin/assimilation-requires-a-resolved-path
@title Assimilation Requires a Reachable and Resolved Path
@sigils [🐜/力]
@keywords accessibility, selection, mutation, path, endpoint, noise, fitness
@audience experiment preregistrars, evolutionary-computation researchers
@tone exacting
@style pattern
@childof baldwin/mechanism
@references [baldwin/assimilable-traits-need-heritable-shadows agent/hypothetical-proof-architecture]

! conclusion:
  A high-function static endpoint is insufficient: the actual genetic operators must
  connect the plastic population to it through steps whose functional loss does not
  exceed their realized learning-cost saving, and evaluation must resolve that margin.

  + context:
    `BaldwinDesign.SelectableAssimilationPath` formalizes the local inequality. In the
    hold-only battery a greedy probe found one selectable extra hold, moving from one to
    two held loci while reach changed from 14.3667 to 14.3333, then stopped because no
    second selectable step existed. Static search ended near reach 1.18 despite known
    static rules with useful dynamics in related protocols.

  + IF:
    A static solution exists somewhere in genome space and plastic genomes achieve high
    function.

  + HOWEVER:
    Endpoint existence says nothing about accessibility from the current lineage.
    Epistasis may require coordinated changes, an early step may cross a valley, a
    coarse band score may erase incremental benefits, and the cost saving per locus may
    lie below evaluation variance.

  + THEN:
    Before evolution, map one-step and short joint rule-plus-hold neighbourhoods around
    representative plastic genomes. Record raw performance loss, realized learning
    saving, uncertainty, and operator probability. Do not launch an assimilation claim
    unless at least one path prefix is accessible, selectable, and statistically
    resolved under the production evaluator.

  + BECAUSE:
    Selection is locally myopic. It cannot choose a distant static rule merely because
    investigators know that rule exists. A step is retainable only when the selected
    fitness difference has the right sign and exceeds stochastic ranking uncertainty.

    + COUNTERFACTUAL:
      If an oracle finds a score-preserving path that the production operator never
      proposes, the bottleneck is mutation supply. If the operator proposes it but
      evaluation cannot rank it, the bottleneck is resolution. If no path exists even
      under joint changes, the representation or target must change.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Use path existence as a gate, not as a post hoc explanation.
    - Report endpoint, accessibility, selectability, and resolution as four separate facts.
